WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.820 --> 00:00:02.560
Hey Youtubers, it's Charlie.

00:00:02.660 --> 00:00:04.500
So, Game of Thrones Episode 1 Q&amp;A.

00:00:04.500 --> 00:00:06.660
Lots of people going crazy about all kinds of stuff.

00:00:06.660 --> 00:00:08.640
Mostly Melisandre - Sand Snake stuff.

00:00:08.640 --> 00:00:11.260
So just careful for spoilers if you haven't seen the episode yet.

00:00:11.260 --> 00:00:13.360
There were a couple questions that everybody had

00:00:13.360 --> 00:00:15.460
so I'll just answer those up front first.

00:00:15.460 --> 00:00:17.980
Melisandre's choker is part of her glamour

00:00:17.980 --> 00:00:23.460
it requires a physical object but glamouring and masking someone's appearance are two different things.

00:00:23.460 --> 00:00:26.000
As you saw, it's a very powerful form of illusion.

00:00:26.000 --> 00:00:26.820
So it's like, wait:

00:00:26.820 --> 00:00:29.160
The time that Stannis and Gendry had sex with her

00:00:29.160 --> 00:00:31.940
Does that mean that they were really having sex with an old woman?

00:00:31.940 --> 00:00:32.840
No.

00:00:32.840 --> 00:00:34.340
It doesn't really work that way.

00:00:34.340 --> 00:00:36.260
Glamour's actually much more powerful than that

00:00:36.260 --> 00:00:38.860
it actually physically changes her body.

00:00:38.860 --> 00:00:41.000
So, when they were having sex with her

00:00:41.000 --> 00:00:44.120
they were actually having sex with this person right here, physically.

00:00:44.120 --> 00:00:44.860
But in reality

00:00:44.860 --> 00:00:45.900
she is ancient.

00:00:45.900 --> 00:00:48.820
But physically in this moment, when she's wearing this glamour

00:00:48.820 --> 00:00:49.860
she's a young person.

00:00:49.860 --> 00:00:52.600
So, one of the really big examples of this in the books

00:00:52.600 --> 00:00:56.040
during Dance with Dragons is when she glamours Mance Rayder

00:00:56.040 --> 00:00:57.860
and you get into the Pink Letter storyline.

00:00:57.860 --> 00:01:01.460
Now because they might do a version of that on the TV show, I don't wanna get into that too much.

00:01:01.460 --> 00:01:04.260
But her taking the glamour off at the end of the episode

00:01:04.260 --> 00:01:06.920
isn't really evidence that her power has gone away.

00:01:06.920 --> 00:01:09.140
She probably does that every once in awhile.

00:01:09.140 --> 00:01:11.400
But I know a lot of you asked about clues in the books

00:01:11.400 --> 00:01:13.380
that say that, y'know maybe she doesn't sleep at all.

00:01:13.380 --> 00:01:16.320
So why is she sleeping if she's not supposed to be sleeping at all?

00:01:16.320 --> 00:01:18.640
I think right now she's just shaken

00:01:18.640 --> 00:01:19.320
so she's like:

00:01:19.320 --> 00:01:21.300
Okay, I need a minute to collect myself.

00:01:21.300 --> 00:01:23.940
So that's why she climbs into bed looking the way she does.

00:01:23.940 --> 00:01:27.500
Otherwise, if Stannis were still alive and sleeping in a room near her

00:01:27.500 --> 00:01:29.640
she would probably keep the glamour on

00:01:29.640 --> 00:01:31.100
or probably wouldn't sleep at all.

00:01:31.100 --> 00:01:31.820
Questions though.

00:01:31.820 --> 00:01:32.420
Here we go.

00:01:32.420 --> 00:01:33.140
First one.

00:01:33.140 --> 00:01:33.880
Juntartful:

00:01:33.880 --> 00:01:36.700
How did the little dagger kill the big dude with the one stab?

00:01:36.700 --> 00:01:40.120
Yeah, it definitely sucked that House Martell went down so fast

00:01:40.120 --> 00:01:42.160
but I think that was just the show telling you

00:01:42.160 --> 00:01:43.740
that they're not that important.

00:01:43.740 --> 00:01:45.040
Like being a cool character

00:01:45.040 --> 00:01:45.920
being important

00:01:45.920 --> 00:01:47.020
two very different things.

00:01:47.020 --> 00:01:50.460
I think the show just decided that it wasn't gonna do a big Martell storyline.

00:01:50.460 --> 00:01:52.020
It wasn't gonna do Master Plan stuff

00:01:52.020 --> 00:01:54.740
so it wanted to tell you in the quickest way possible

00:01:54.740 --> 00:01:57.060
that they were just gonna move on to something else.

00:01:57.100 --> 00:01:57.840
So it's like:

00:01:57.840 --> 00:01:59.340
Okay, yeah these are important characters

00:01:59.360 --> 00:02:00.720
but this is our way of telling you

00:02:00.720 --> 00:02:03.400
that they're not gonna be important in the long scheme of things.

00:02:03.400 --> 00:02:05.560
I think the even more upsetting thing though

00:02:05.560 --> 00:02:09.300
is that they made Doran Martell seem like a really boring character.

00:02:09.300 --> 00:02:12.120
Like, he pretends to be boring because of his gout

00:02:12.120 --> 00:02:13.560
he can't move so he seems really feeble.

00:02:13.560 --> 00:02:16.340
He uses that to his advantage when he's dealing with other people

00:02:16.340 --> 00:02:17.620
because they underestimate him

00:02:17.620 --> 00:02:21.420
but what the show has done, is turn him from a person who pretends be boring

00:02:21.420 --> 00:02:23.200
to a person who is actually boring.

00:02:23.200 --> 00:02:27.600
And I think that's more worthy of complaint than say like the Sand Snakes getting on the boat with Trystane.

00:02:27.600 --> 00:02:28.540
Speaking of which.

00:02:28.540 --> 00:02:29.040
Next question

00:02:29.040 --> 00:02:29.800
Chriser asks:

00:02:29.800 --> 00:02:32.940
Anyone know how the Sand Snakes ended up on the boat with Trystane?

00:02:32.980 --> 00:02:35.140
So, there was a big question about this.

00:02:35.140 --> 00:02:36.300
Y'know, which boat was he on?

00:02:36.300 --> 00:02:37.680
Was he on the boat with Jaime?

00:02:37.680 --> 00:02:40.120
So, I think that he was on a different boat

00:02:40.120 --> 00:02:41.200
just to explain that.

00:02:41.200 --> 00:02:42.260
At the end of last season

00:02:42.260 --> 00:02:45.200
it seemed like he got on the same boat as Jaime and Myrcella.

00:02:45.200 --> 00:02:47.020
So that's why everybody was really confused.

00:02:47.020 --> 00:02:48.580
Wait, if they were on the boat with Jaime

00:02:48.580 --> 00:02:51.300
then how come Jaime didn't say anything about it to Cersei?

00:02:51.300 --> 00:02:52.960
How come we didn't see any interaction there?

00:02:52.960 --> 00:02:55.200
I think the easiest answer that makes sense

00:02:55.200 --> 00:02:58.060
is that he just escorted Myrcella onto that boat

00:02:58.060 --> 00:02:59.140
then he turned around

00:02:59.140 --> 00:03:00.060
came back to dock

00:03:00.060 --> 00:03:01.220
and took a different ship.

00:03:01.220 --> 00:03:03.660
So that's not necessarily the best explanation

00:03:03.660 --> 00:03:04.920
but that's the best one I can think of.

00:03:04.920 --> 00:03:10.500
He was on a different boat and when he got on that different boat the Sand Snakes also got on that boat with him.

00:03:10.500 --> 00:03:12.780
Like, he thought initially that they were travelling him

00:03:12.780 --> 00:03:15.940
because he wasn't surprised to see them when they first walked into his room.

00:03:15.940 --> 00:03:17.680
He didn't think anything weird was going on.

00:03:17.680 --> 00:03:18.660
Next question

00:03:18.660 --> 00:03:19.460
Fish Tank Girl asks:

00:03:19.460 --> 00:03:22.260
In the beginning of the episode when Jon's body is removed from the ground

00:03:22.260 --> 00:03:25.480
Davos looks really long at the place where his body was lying

00:03:25.480 --> 00:03:26.640
it must mean something.

00:03:26.640 --> 00:03:29.060
They seem a point of making sure that you notice

00:03:29.060 --> 00:03:32.820
he looks really long at the impression of Jon Snow's body in the snow

00:03:32.820 --> 00:03:34.620
foreshadowing for something.

00:03:34.620 --> 00:03:38.980
Yeah, so the show has to do things in a visual way that you wouldn't necessarily do in the books.

00:03:38.980 --> 00:03:40.340
Like, the books have POV chapters

00:03:40.340 --> 00:03:41.860
so when you wanna foreshadow something

00:03:41.860 --> 00:03:43.740
you just have a character think about that

00:03:43.740 --> 00:03:45.900
but you can't really do that on the TV show.

00:03:45.900 --> 00:03:49.280
Usually when the camera lingers on something it can mean a couple different things

00:03:49.280 --> 00:03:50.680
but in the case of Jon Snow's body

00:03:50.680 --> 00:03:53.160
just - because we all have this theory that he's coming back

00:03:53.160 --> 00:03:55.140
we definitely think that they're foreshadowing that

00:03:55.140 --> 00:03:57.220
and I do agree that's what they're foreshadowing.

00:03:57.220 --> 00:03:59.420
Like, this isn't as simple as it seems.

00:03:59.420 --> 00:04:03.200
There were a couple storylines in the episode where they talked about dead bodies.

00:04:03.200 --> 00:04:05.580
You have Cersei talking about her mother's dead body

00:04:05.580 --> 00:04:06.520
about how it turns black

00:04:06.520 --> 00:04:08.020
talking about Myrcella's body.

00:04:08.020 --> 00:04:12.240
Then you have Ramsay standing over Myranda's dead body for a couple minutes before he's like:

00:04:12.240 --> 00:04:13.320
Yep, feed her to the dogs.

00:04:13.320 --> 00:04:16.700
So one - the fact that no-one has talked about burning Jon Snow's body

00:04:16.700 --> 00:04:17.660
or it decaying

00:04:17.660 --> 00:04:18.640
or anything like that

00:04:18.640 --> 00:04:20.420
tells you a lot that you need to know.

00:04:20.420 --> 00:04:22.040
Like, he's just gonna be chilling here

00:04:22.040 --> 00:04:23.180
waiting for something.

00:04:23.180 --> 00:04:25.240
Most of what's gonna happen with his body

00:04:25.240 --> 00:04:28.160
I think will come through Bran's character via flashbacks

00:04:28.160 --> 00:04:29.160
like Tower of Joy stuff

00:04:29.160 --> 00:04:31.040
and Melisandre in present day.

00:04:31.040 --> 00:04:33.140
So just watch for the next couple of episodes.

00:04:33.140 --> 00:04:36.660
There's still gonna be a lot of suspense surrounding what's going on with him.

00:04:36.660 --> 00:04:37.160
Next question

00:04:37.160 --> 00:04:37.800
Justin asks:

00:04:37.800 --> 00:04:41.000
What about the stuff with the religious group? Is that in the books at all?

00:04:41.000 --> 00:04:43.400
Well, there are other Red Priests in Meereen

